    {
      "key": "about",
      "title": "About the Journal",
      "bodyHtml": "<p>Transient – A Journal of Natural Science and Allied Subjects, is an annual peer reviewed multi-discipline research science journal (ISSN NO. 2250-0650) in English published by Don Bosco College, Tura, Meghalaya, India from the year 2011. The types of contributions accepted are categorized as strategy articles, review articles, research articles, short communications and maiden reports. The Journal is visualized as a forum to publish and interchange experiment-based ideas, critical views on scientific issues and express crucial ideas on the beneficial applications of modern science in contemporary society. It is further envisaged that through this journal young scholars may widen their avenues to publish their findings through this national journal. All submissions are reviewed by experts/peers and the Editorial Committee and on their recommendation, manuscripts are published.</p><p><strong>Publisher:</strong> Don Bosco College, Tura, West Garo Hills, Meghalaya-794002</p><p><strong>Academic correspondence:</strong> Dr. Yubaraj Sharma, Chief Editor, Transient, Don Bosco College, Tura, 794002, Meghalaya, India. Email: <a href=\"mailto:transient@donboscocollege.ac.in\">transient@donboscocollege.ac.in</a></p>",
      "seoTitle": "About Transient Journal",
      "seoDescription": "About Transient (ISSN 2250-0650) — peer-reviewed journal of natural sciences published by Don Bosco College, Tura.",
      "seoKeywords": ["2250-0650", "Transient", "about"]
    },
    {
      "key": "chief-editor-message",
      "title": "From the Chief Editor's desk",
      "bodyHtml": "<p>The journal Transient is an attempt to provide a platform for researchers in different fields of science to showcase their research; an endeavour along the line of numerous other international, national and regional journals. The rationale for adding one more to the list of existing journals is that a lot of scientific research goes unpublished for the simple reason that most journals put great emphasis on the significance of the results or conclusions drawn from a particular research work; the exclusion of research, however simple or basic, from visible literature might lead researchers to keep on 'reinventing the wheel' causing loss of precious time. In Transient, we try to honour the endeavour and hard work put out by researchers in carrying out their work even though the outcome might not be 'paradigm-changing' by giving due recognition, without sacrificing scientific rigour, to the merits of the scientific content and methods of an article.</p><p>I am pleased to inform the release of the preprints of the Xth volume of the Journal. This special volume is meticulously curated from the submissions to the International Seminar, \"Climate Change: Impact and Resilience\" that was organized by Assam Don Bosco University (ADBU).</p><p>We are now inviting manuscripts for the XIth volume of Transient.</p><p><em>Dr. Yubaraj Sharma</em></p>",
      "seoTitle": "Chief Editor's Message — Transient",
      "seoDescription": "Message from the Chief Editor of Transient journal.",
      "seoKeywords": ["chief editor", "Transient"]
    },
